    "angular: typescript/consistent-type-imports": "The autofix turns the import of an injected class into `import type`. Constructor injection needs the class at runtime (`emitDecoratorMetadata` records it as the parameter's type), so the fix compiles and then fails to resolve the dependency.",
    "core: import/consistent-type-specifier-style": "── import ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────",
    "core: no-unused-vars": "One convention for \"unused on purpose\" in every linter: a leading underscore, for parameters, variables, caught errors and destructured array elements. A property left out through a rest sibling (`const { secret, ...rest } = obj`) and a `using` declaration held only for its disposal aren't unused either.",
    "core: unicorn/prefer-export-from": "Off until oxlint's fix is corrected: its suggestion, which `--fix-suggestions` and `--fix-dangerously` apply, rewrites `import { a } from \"./x\"; import { b } from \"./y\"; export { a, b };` to `export { a } from \"./x\";` and drops the export of `b` (https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc/issues/29318). The ESLint preset keeps the rule, whose fix is correct.",
    "nestjs: typescript/consistent-type-imports": "The autofix turns the import of an injected class into `import type`. Constructor injection needs the class at runtime (`emitDecoratorMetadata` records it as the parameter's type), so the fix compiles and then fails to resolve the dependency."
